instruction:
URGENT CLEANUP + VERIFICATION in the Go repo at /gin. Time is short; be fast and precise.

Step 1: Delete all leftover scratch/temporary test files that subagents created in the repo root, i.e. any untracked file matching /gin/zz_*.go and any other untracked *.go files that are NOT part of the original repository. Verify with `cd /gin && git status --porcelain`. The ONLY modified tracked file allowed to remain is response_writer.go (and possibly errors.go, tree.go, context.go if other subagents fixed them). Do NOT delete or revert any tracked file's changes.

Step 2: Check whether /gin/errors.go still contains the bug: the method `func (msg Error) Error() string` has a VALUE receiver. The doc comment on `Unwrap` promises interoperability with errors.Is/errors.As/errors.Unwrap, and `var _ error = &Error{}` plus the standard library require `Error()` to have a POINTER receiver `func (msg *Error) Error() string` so that a `*Error` value wrapped via fmt.Errorf("%w") unwraps correctly. If it is still a value receiver, change it to a pointer receiver: `func (msg *Error) Error() string { return msg.Err.Error() }`. Then run `cd /gin && go build ./... && go test -count=1 -run 'TestError' -v .` and also write a TEMPORARY test file /gin/zz_tmp_unwrap_test.go containing exactly:

package gin

import (
	"errors"
	"fmt"
	"testing"
)

type tmpTestErr string

func (e tmpTestErr) Error() string { return string(e) }

func TestTmpUnwrap(t *testing.T) {
	innerErr := tmpTestErr("some error")
	err := fmt.Errorf("wrapped: %w", &Error{Err: innerErr, Type: ErrorTypeAny})
	if !errors.Is(err, innerErr) { t.Fatal("errors.Is failed") }
	var te tmpTestErr
	if !errors.As(err, &te) { t.Fatal("errors.As failed") }
}

Run `cd /gin && go test -count=1 -run TestTmpUnwrap -v .`, then DELETE that temp file. If the test fails, report the exact failure and try the minimal fix that makes it pass (likely the pointer receiver above).

Step 3: Run the FULL suite: `cd /gin && go build ./... && go vet ./... && go test -count=1 ./... 2>&1 | tail -30`. Make sure no scratch files remain afterwards (`git status --porcelain`).

Report: the final `git status --porcelain`, the exact diff of every tracked file changed (`git diff`), and the final full-suite result. Do not leave any zz_*.go files behind.
